# The assessment of COR-EXEC-006 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# COR-EXEC-006: "Each operation shall declare its rollback boundary and whether reversal
# is Exact, Compensating, RepositoryRecoverable, ProviderDependent, or Irreversible.
# Parallel groups shall not cross incompatible rollback boundaries."
#
# First sentence: genuinely met. CommittedPlan::Rollback_Boundary is real and tested --
# not unconsumed vocabulary sitting beside a real operation, but the declaration a real,
# exercised operation (CommittedPlan::Rollback) makes about itself, provably Exact by
# construction and asserted by
# Test_A_Committed_Plan_Declares_An_Exact_Rollback_Boundary.
#
# Second sentence: a constraint on a parallel-group scheduler this crate does not have --
# CorrectionPlan runs one plan at a time -- the same second-sentence carve-out
# RankingCriterion's own doc comment already draws for COR-011's second sentence: a
# constraint on a future function, not an obligation this type itself owes.
verdict: Met
site: crates/corrections/nomos-corrections/src/committed_plan.rs#Rollback_Boundary
